(6) Vote in matters before the city council to the extent provided in subsection (a) of section 2.10 of this Charter;
(7) Make all appointments of city officers as provided by this Charter, subject to confirmation by the city council;
(8) Serve in a part-time capacity and be compensated accordingly; and
(9) Perform any other duties and exercise any other powers required by state or federal law or authorized by a duly adopted ordinance that is not in conflict with this Charter.
(b) The mayor shall have all of the powers specifically granted to the mayor elsewhere in this Charter regardless of whether such powers are enumerated in this section.
